import Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Pointwise.Set.Basic
import Mathlib.GroupTheory.GroupAction.Defs

/-!
# Abstract Lorentzian spacetime interface

This file provides the abstract interface over which the Haag-Kastler
axioms in *curved* (Lorentzian) spacetime are formalised, following
Chapter 10 of the AQFT-in-Lean blueprint (`def:lorentzian-spacetime` in
`sec10/spacetime` and the `*-in-curved-spacetime` declarations in
`sec10/haag-kastler-axioms-in-curved-spacetime`). The expository
narrative is the separate Chapter 9 ("Haag Kastler Axioms in Curved
Spacetime").

The blueprint's `def:lorentzian-spacetime` describes a smooth,
connected, four-dimensional Hausdorff manifold equipped with a
smooth nowhere-vanishing global vector field, an associated
Lorentzian metric, and a Hausdorff Alexandrov topology. Building
that differential-geometric object in full (chronological future /
past via timelike curves, the Alexandrov topology generated by the
diamonds `I⁺(p) ∩ I⁻(q)`, etc.) is a substantial undertaking.

Following the *axioms-first* strategy, this file does **not**
construct that object. Instead it isolates the *interface* that the
five axioms actually use:

* a type of spacetime points `Carrier`;
* a predicate `IsBasisSet` picking out the Alexandrov-basis
  "diamonds" `𝐁 = I⁺(p) ∩ I⁻(q)`;
* a binary predicate `IsCompletelySpacelike` on basis sets, used by
  Axiom 3 (Local Commutativity);
* a group `Isom` of *isometries connected to the identity* together
  with its action on `Carrier`, used by Axiom 5 (Isometric
  Covariance);
* `isBasisSet_smul`, witnessing that those isometries carry basis sets
  to basis sets.

The geometric bundle `Physicslib4.Spacetime.LorentzianSpacetime`
instantiates this interface via `toAbstractIdentityComponent`
(`Concrete.lean`); the axioms and any consequences proved here
transfer verbatim.

## Modelling notes

* The `Group`/`MulAction` data for the isometry group is stored as
  ordinary structure fields and re-exposed as instances via
  `attribute [instance]`, mirroring the `LocalNet.instCStarAlgebra`
  pattern. With `open Pointwise`, the pointwise action
  `MulAction M.Isom (Set M.Carrier)` (i.e. `φ • 𝐁 = φ(𝐁)`) is then
  available automatically.
* `Carrier` and `Isom` are universe-polymorphic so that a concrete
  spacetime in any universe (e.g. `Physicslib4.Spacetime`, whose
  carrier is `Type*`) can instantiate the interface. The local
  algebras assigned by `LocalNet.{u, v}` live in a universe `v`
  independent of the universe `u` of `Carrier`, and the GNS Hilbert
  spaces of Axiom 4 (and of the GNS results built on the net) live in
  the same universe `v` as the algebras, as in the Minkowski net.
-/

namespace Physicslib4
namespace AQFT
namespace HaagKastlerCurved

open scoped Pointwise

universe u

/--
The abstract Lorentzian spacetime: exactly the structure that the curved-spacetime axioms use.

The curved Haag–Kastler axioms never look at the metric directly. They need the points of the
spacetime M; the causal diamonds B = I⁺(p) ∩ I⁻(q), which are the basis sets of the Alexandrov
topology; the relation "B₁ and B₂ are completely spacelike", used by Axiom 3; and the group of
isometries of M connected to the identity with its action on points, used by Axiom 5. The
interface records these, together with the one fact Axiom 5 needs: an isometry φ carries a basis
set B to a basis set φ(B), so that α_φ : 𝔘(B) → 𝔘(φ(B)) is a map between local algebras of basis
sets.

The interface imposes no other conditions on these pieces. A geometric Lorentzian spacetime
(`Physicslib4.Spacetime.LorentzianSpacetime`: a connected four-dimensional manifold with a
Lorentzian metric, a time orientation and a Hausdorff Alexandrov topology) gives an instance
through `Physicslib4.Spacetime.LorentzianSpacetime.toAbstractIdentityComponent`, and every result
proved over the interface applies to it.

Implementation note: the group structure and the action are fields, declared instances once the
interface is defined, so that with `open Pointwise` the image φ(B) is written `φ • B`. The points
and the isometries live in one universe u.

Blueprint: def:abstract-lorentzian-spacetime-interface
-/
structure LorentzianSpacetime where
  /-- The points of the spacetime M. -/
  Carrier : Type u
  /-- The basis sets of the Alexandrov topology: the causal diamonds I⁺(p) ∩ I⁻(q). These are the
  regions to which the axioms attach local algebras. -/
  IsBasisSet : Set Carrier → Prop
  /-- Complete spacelike separation of two regions, under which Axiom 3 makes their algebras
  commute. For a geometric spacetime it holds when every point of the one region is spacelike to
  every point of the other. -/
  IsCompletelySpacelike : Set Carrier → Set Carrier → Prop
  /-- The group of isometries of M connected to the identity: the symmetry group of Axiom 5. -/
  Isom : Type u
  /-- The group structure of the isometries: composition, identity and inverse. -/
  instGroup : Group Isom
  /-- The action φ • x = φ(x) of the isometries on the points of M. -/
  instAction : MulAction Isom Carrier
  /-- An isometry carries basis sets to basis sets, so that the Axiom 5 map
  α_φ : 𝔘(B) → 𝔘(φ(B)) is a map between local algebras of basis sets. -/
  isBasisSet_smul : ∀ (φ : Isom) {B : Set Carrier}, IsBasisSet B → IsBasisSet (φ • B)

attribute [instance] LorentzianSpacetime.instGroup LorentzianSpacetime.instAction

end HaagKastlerCurved
end AQFT
end Physicslib4
